Z||000001||loafer87gt||07-09-2001||07:23 PM||||IS it throwing any codes (the check engine light coming on?) I suspect it could just be a gunked up throttle linkage cable. I used graphite brake cleaner and sprayed the linkage by the throttle body and it fixed the problem. An easy way to tell if it is your throttle linkage that is causing the problem is when you start your car and it revs high, pull the gas pedal towards you and if the revs drops thats the culprit.||||reg||1
