Z||000003||fierohoho||07-10-2001||01:13 AM||||I had a similar problem with a '86 2.5L (you neglected to say what motor you have)and found that the coolant was low causing the ECM temp sensor to be high and dry. The engine would rev presumably to help it6 get up to operating temp. When I topped off the coolant my idle dropped to normal. Something to check anyhow. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
